  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Restoring Dignity and Justice in Ukraine: A Whole-Of-Government Approach to Advancing Accountability for International Crimes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen survivor-centred and trauma-informed capacities in investigation and prosecution of conflict-related sexual violence. 2) To strengthen the capacities of the Office of the Prosecutor General and regional prosecution offices&#x2019; in handling crimes against and affecting children. 3) To assess progress along institutional reform priorities. 4) To inform policy dialogue through validated assessment results and recommendations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Office of the Prosecutor General, the National Police of Ukraine.Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers, particularly survivors and child victims of international crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to advance accountability for international crimes committed in Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
